  "term": "theoretical orientation",
  "definition": "Theoretical orientation is the broad conceptual approach or perspective a framework is based on. In process evaluation, it helps classify frameworks and influences which aspects of implementation are emphasized, what questions are asked, and how findings are interpreted.",
